  "id": "COMPOUND:38301 - PROTEIN:5832",
  "verbalization": "Hedaol B is shown to have a target relationship with Raji, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including (6R)-2-methyl-6-(4-methylphenyl)hept-2-en-4-ol, Maplexin A, and terbutaline. All of these compounds ultimately target HuT78, suggesting a shared mechanism of action or a common pathway leading to the effect on HuT78. The evidence indicates that Hedaol B may influence Raji through these intermediaries, potentially modulating biological processes that result in the interaction with HuT78. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Hedaol B in regulating cellular functions that are relevant to HuT78, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
